so far critics and audiences alike seem  to be responding positively to zack  snyder's army of the dead  praising the genre-bending zombie movie  for its premise  its heart and its over-the-top action  sequences  the story follows a ragtag group of  mercenaries led by dave bautista's  scott wood as they travel through an  undead ridden las vegas in an effort to  retrieve a mountain of loot from a  casino vault  one of the most important members in  this carnage causing posse  is marianne peters a cigar chomping  helicopter pilot who's tasked with  safely flying the team out of the city  after the mission is complete 100 i  meant  yeah you don't want to know you know the  risks or why would i want to know the  risks  originally the comedian chris de lea was  supposed to play the pilot character  in army of the dead but he was fired  from the movie after becoming the  subject of investigations  into alleged sexual misconduct while  delia denies any wrongdoing  snyder and company had no reservations  about replacing him  in a recent interview with vanity fair  snyder revealed that the decision to  replace dalia was a fairly easy one  he also believes that tig notaro's  presence did a lot more than just make  some distance between the movie  and delia's scandals in fact the snyder  said that notaro's performance brought a  whole new unexpected dimension to the  film  the director explained i think the movie  is better with tig notaro  frankly because she's more unexpected  and she's more fun while they were  eventually able to turn their obstacle  into an opportunity  the filmmakers were very much aware of  the risks that came with replacing dalia  so late into the production according to  schneider the situation could have been  a disaster  if he didn't have the right team in  place fortunately his colleagues are  used to working on visual effects heavy  blockbusters  and so they eventually managed to  successfully replace taliyah without  making it too obvious in the final cut  but it certainly wasn't easy in fact  having to replace dalia with notaro gave  the filmmakers all kinds of headaches  first they had to erase every mention of  delia's character  and digitally insert tignotaro into the  scenes instead given that the situation  unfolded during the pandemic  reshooting the scenes with the actors  together wasn't an option  so they had to get creative and spend a  lot of money  during her interview with vanity fair  deborah snyder revealed that the cost of  adding the new actor  was equivalent to the entire budget for  army of thieves  the upcoming prequel to army of the dead  however  both she and her husband credited  netflix for doing the right thing  by putting their money where their mouth  is nataro's own health issues also posed  a problem for the snyders and their crew  as a cancer survivor it wouldn't  typically have been advisable for notaro  to make any movies during a pandemic  indeed deborah snyder admitted that  notaro was nervous about her health  potentially being compromised  but she pressed ahead with the project  anyway and thankfully didn't encounter  any issues during the shoot  of course some of notaro scenes in army  of the dead were obviously the product  of some expert digital wizardry  but at the moment really do make it seem  like she was part of the movie  the entire time in one scene that snyder  would soon have to cut  though taro is featured speaking to dave  bautista's character  as he leads the mercenaries down a  corridor he told vanity fair  when we first talked about it i was like  this is gonna be really hard because  they're all backlit and haloed  and there's a lens flare but it came out  perfectly i'm not trying to be the bad  guy  we should be incentivized to let him die  funnily enough while batista and notaro  have some surprisingly great chemistry  with each other in army of the dead  the former wwe champion still hasn't  been formally introduced to his co-star  while speaking to 